<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Spartrak head assets.

  The <remove> block below strips assets that Smartwave/porto's own
  Magento_Theme/layout/default_head_blocks.xml adds to every page and that
  this theme inherits. Each removal was verified against the rendered output
  of the live homepage, PDP, category and search pages — the class prefixes
  these files define do not appear anywhere in that markup:

      owl.carousel.css        4.7KB   "owl-"        0 occurrences
      simple-line-icons.css  12.1KB   "simple-line" 0 occurrences
      font-awesome.min.css    8.5KB   "fa-"         0 occurrences
      Shadows Into Light              a decorative Google script face, absent
                                      from _typography.less's stack
                                      (thmanyah sans / Inter / Inter Tight)

  The font link costs more than its byte count suggests: it is a separate
  DNS + TLS + request to a third-party host, on an origin currently serving
  HTTP/1.1, so it competes for the per-host connection budget rather than
  multiplexing.

  ===========================================================================
  SECOND PASS, 2026-09-05 (performance audit)
  ===========================================================================
  Three more files, each re-verified against the LIVE rendered output of four
  page types before being listed - homepage, PDP (sp-2218), a CMS/contact page
  and the cart:

      fancybox/css/jquery.fancybox.css        3,923B   "fancybox"   0 / 0 / 0 / 0
      Smartwave_Filterproducts owl.carousel  10,285B   "owl-carousel" 0 / 0 / 0 / 0
      Smartwave_Dailydeals::css/style.css     1,537B   "dailydeal"  0 / 0 / 0 / 0

  fancybox: the previous note kept it because "fancybox" appeared 20x in
  inline JS config strings. It appears ZERO times now. Its only consumer in
  this codebase is Porto's Magento_Newsletter/templates/subscribe_popup.phtml,
  which is gated on `porto_settings/newsletter/enable` and emits nothing on
  this install - the popup markup is absent from all four pages. Porto's own
  default_head_blocks.xml already has the matching fancybox <script> line
  commented out, so the stylesheet was styling a lightbox that cannot open.

  Smartwave_Filterproducts: its default.xml adds a SECOND copy of owl.carousel
  to every page - Porto's own copy of the same library was already removed
  above, so this was the duplicate that survived. Nothing in Spartrak
  references a Filterproducts widget or block, and no `.owl-carousel` element
  renders anywhere.

  Smartwave_Dailydeals: its default.xml adds this to every page for a Daily
  Deals surface that does not render on any of them.

  ===========================================================================
  THIRD PASS, 2026-09-06 — the porto-icons font, removed outright
  ===========================================================================
  The note that used to sit here kept porto-icons-codes.css because the PDP
  and contact page "render seven porto-icon-* classes". They do carry those
  classes. Six of the seven turned out not to matter, and the rule that DID
  matter was not among them.

  Measured on the live site with getComputedStyle over every element and both
  pseudo-elements, rather than by reading markup:

      PDP  i.porto-icon-up-dir / -down-dir / em.-right-open   box 0x0, NOT rendered
      PDP  div.reviews-actions:before                         238x24, RENDERED
      contact  i.porto-icon-phone / -mobile / -mail-alt / -skype  43x43, RENDERED
      homepage, cart                                          nothing rendered

  The three PDP classes were already collapsed to zero by this theme's own
  CSS - and the font downloaded on the PDP regardless, pulled by Porto's
  five-empty-star review placeholder, which nobody had listed. Checkout does
  the same through a rule still unnamed. That is the point: a glyph does not
  have to be one we put there, or one we can name, to cost 63,304 bytes.

  So the fix is not a page scope, it is deletion. web/css/source/_icons.less
  no longer declares the @font-face at all, which makes `font-family:
  porto-icons` resolve to no font on every page at once, whatever the
  selector. The five marks measured as visible are re-drawn as Spartrak SVGs
  in web/css/source/components/_porto-icon-retirement.less.

      icon-fonts/css/porto-icons-codes.css   13.1KB   removed below
      icon-fonts/css/animation.css            1.5KB   removed below
      icon-fonts/font/porto-icons.woff2      63.3KB   no longer referenced

  animation.css goes with it. All 85 lines of it are one `.animate-spin` class
  and the `spin` keyframes behind it. Its only consumers in this codebase are
  Porto's Smartwave_Porto/templates/ajaxproducts/*.phtml and fancybox's JS,
  and both write it as `<i class="ajax-loader large animate-spin">` - i.e. it
  exists to rotate an icon-FONT glyph, which no longer has a glyph to rotate.
  `animate-spin` appears zero times in the rendered homepage, PDP, contact and
  cart, and fancybox's own stylesheet was already removed in the second pass
  above as "styling a lightbox that cannot open".

  This does NOT touch the Spartrak loader: components/_loader.less owns that,
  it is pure CSS on Spartrak markup, and it shares no class or keyframe name
  with this file.
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <head>
        <remove src="owl.carousel/assets/owl.carousel.css"/>
        <remove src="simple-line-icons/css/simple-line-icons.css"/>
        <remove src="font-awesome/css/font-awesome.min.css"/>
        <remove src="//fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Shadows+Into+Light"/>
        <remove src="fancybox/css/jquery.fancybox.css"/>
        <remove src="Smartwave_Filterproducts::css/owl.carousel/assets/owl.carousel.css"/>
        <remove src="Smartwave_Dailydeals::css/style.css"/>
        <remove src="icon-fonts/css/porto-icons-codes.css"/>
        <remove src="icon-fonts/css/animation.css"/>

        <css src="css/spartrak-foundations.css"/>
        <css src="css/spartrak-components.css"/>
    </head>
</page>
